        "rtf_UTiq3g": {
          "type": "rtf",
          "settings": {
            "richtext_content": "<p>Ross Edgley is a world-renowned endurance athlete, author, and adventurer known for pushing the boundaries of human performance. With numerous world records under his belt, including being the first person to swim around Great Britain, Ross embodies the Gym King ethos of resilience, dedication, and breaking limits. As a proud Gym King ambassador, Ross inspires others to embrace challenges and pursue greatness in every aspect of life.</p>"
          }
        },
        "video_dx9fM3": {
          "type": "video",
          "settings": {
            "linked_video": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ETDJ44zMGeQ"
          }
        },
        "rtf_7bBxeU": {
          "type": "rtf",
          "settings": {
            "richtext_content": "<h1>Career Highlights</h1><h3>2015: Strongman Swimming</h3><p>Completed a 100km swim while towing a 100lb tree, combining strength and endurance in a world-first challenge.</p><h3>2016: Guinness World Record - Rope Climbing</h3><p>Climbed 8,848m on a rope - the equivalent height of Mount Everest - in just 19 hours, setting a Guinness World Record.</p><h3>2016: Marathon While Pulling a Car</h3><p>Completed a 26.2-mile marathon while pulling a 1.4-ton car, pushing the limits of strength and endurance.</p><h3>2018: First Person to Swim Around Great Britain</h3><p>Became the first person to swim around the entire coastline of Great Britain. Over 157 days, Ross covered 1,780 miles without setting foot on land.</p><h3>2024: Longest Non-Stop River Swim</h3><p>Set a Guinness World Record by swimming 510km down Canada’s Yukon River in 54 hours and 45 minutes without stopping, sleeping or touching the support boat.</p><h3>2025: First Person to Swim Around Iceland</h3><p>Completed the first swim around the entire coastline of Iceland, covering more than 1,000 miles over 114 days. The expedition saw Ross battle freezing waters, huge waves and extreme weather while collecting vital ocean conservation data.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
